---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Demo from "../components/Demo.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Rotagivan — Life at lightning speed"
  description="Put your Mac in motion. Explore Rotagivan’s radial HUD, custom gestures, app shortcuts, and multi-step macros in an interactive demo."
>
  <section class="hero wrap">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">
        <span class="tiny-bolt" aria-hidden="true">
          ϟ
        </span>{" "}
        A NEW RHYTHM FOR YOUR MAC
      </p>
      <h1>
        Life at
        <br />
        <em>lightning</em>
        <br />
        speed<span class="lime">.</span>
      </h1>
      <p class="lede">
        The thought. The gesture. Done.
        <br />
        Bring your apps, shortcuts, and everyday routines into one effortless
        motion.
      </p>
      <div class="button-row">
        <a class="button" href="#playground">
          Feel the flow <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
        </a>
        <a class="quiet-link" href="/download/">
          Meet Rotagivan
        </a>
      </div>
      <p class="hero-note">Built for macOS · Designed around you</p>
    </div>
    <div class="hero-demo" id="playground">
      <Demo />
      <span class="demo-caption">
        LESS REACHING. LESS SEARCHING. MORE DOING.
      </span>
    </div>
  </section>
  <div class="capability-strip">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span>
        One wheel.
        <br />
        <strong>So many possibilities.</strong>
      </span>
      <span>App launching</span>
      <span>Custom gestures</span>
      <span>Window control</span>
      <span>Multi-step macros</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <section class="section wrap" id="how-it-works">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">01 / CLOSE THE GAP</p>
      <h2>
        Your ideas move fast.
        <br />
        <span class="muted">Your Mac should keep up.</span>
      </h2>
      <p>
        Every menu hunt breaks the rhythm. Rotagivan puts your next action where
        you already are—on a wheel you make your own.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="steps">
      <article>
        <span class="step-number">01</span>
        <h3>Make it yours.</h3>
        <p>
          Place your favorite apps, websites, and actions on the HUD. Group them
          the way you think.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span class="step-number">02</span>
        <h3>Find your gesture.</h3>
        <p>
          Assign a hotkey or trackpad gesture. Call up your controls without
          retracing the same menus.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span class="step-number">03</span>
        <h3>Stay in the flow.</h3>
        <p>
          Choose your next move. Launch, arrange, or run a sequence—and get
          right back to the work.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="feature-section wrap">
    <div class="feature-card wide">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">02 / LESS BUSYWORK</p>
        <h2>
          One action.
          <br />A whole head start.
        </h2>
        <p>
          Opening an app is just the beginning. Chain app launches and
          keystrokes into a named macro. Turn the setup you repeat into a
          routine you can reach.
        </p>
        <a class="quiet-link" href="#playground">
          Try Focus on the wheel <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
        </a>
      </div>
      <div
        class="macro-visual"
        aria-label="Example macro: Open writing app, send focus shortcut, start writing"
      >
        <div class="macro-trigger">
          <span>ϟ</span> Start writing <kbd>⌥ W</kbd>
        </div>
        <div class="macro-step">
          <b>01</b>
          <span>
            Open your writing app
            <small>The right place, already in focus.</small>
          </span>
          <span>✓</span>
        </div>
        <div class="macro-step">
          <b>02</b>
          <span>
            Send your focus shortcut
            <small>Your preferred setup, in sequence.</small>
          </span>
          <span>✓</span>
        </div>
        <div class="macro-result">
          The blank page is waiting.
          <span class="cursor-line" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </div>
        <small class="fineprint">
          Example configuration. You choose the apps and shortcuts.
        </small>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="feature-card">
      <p class="eyebrow">YOUR MUSCLE MEMORY</p>
      <h3>
        A shortcut that
        <br />
        feels like second nature.
      </h3>
      <p>
        Use keyboard hotkeys or Navigator gestures. Tune Navigator pointer
        response and calibrate timing to the way you move.
      </p>
      <div class="key-combo" aria-hidden="true">
        <kbd>⌥</kbd>
        <kbd>⇧</kbd>
        <kbd>Space</kbd>
        <span>→</span>
        <span class="key-wheel">ϟ</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="feature-card">
      <p class="eyebrow">YOUR CONTEXT</p>
      <h3>
        Same Mac.
        <br />
        Different headspace.
      </h3>
      <p>
        Build profiles and layers for writing, creating, or daily work. Add
        app-specific actions that belong to the task in front of you.
      </p>
      <div class="profile-pills" aria-label="Example profile names">
        <span>⌘ Work</span>
        <span>✳ Create</span>
        <span>◎ Focus</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section wrap compatibility">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">03 / FIND YOUR SETUP</p>
      <h2>
        Built around
        <br />
        <em>your next move.</em>
      </h2>
    </div>
    <div class="compat-list">
      <article>
        <span>⌘</span>
        <div>
          <h3>Keyboard, meet command center.</h3>
          <p>Bring actions and HUD layers to your favorite hotkeys.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span>⌁</span>
        <div>
          <h3>Made for ZSA Navigator.</h3>
          <p>
            Direct touch input, custom gestures, and pointer tuning. Current
            hardware verification centers on Voyager.
          </p>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span>◈</span>
        <div>
          <h3>Apple trackpad, too. Experimentally.</h3>
          <p>
            Optional gesture actions for supported Apple trackpads. macOS keeps
            control of normal pointing and scrolling.
          </p>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span>≋</span>
        <div>
          <h3>A voice when you want it.</h3>
          <p>
            Speak a command, review a suggestion, and confirm. Optional cloud
            voice features require provider credentials.
          </p>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="closing wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">LESS BETWEEN YOU AND YOUR NEXT IDEA.</p>
    <h2>
      Make your next move
      <br />
      <em>your best move.</em>
    </h2>
    <div class="button-row">
      <a class="button" href="#playground">
        Take the wheel <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
      </a>
      <a class="quiet-link" href="/pricing/">
        Explore pricing
      </a>
    </div>
    <p class="fineprint">
      Rotagivan is in development. Public release details are coming soon.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>
